. LESSON 9 MORE ON GRAPHICS
. SNAP copies part of the screen into a picture, and DISPLAY puts it
. back anywhere, in displaymode 0 plop, 1 XOR, 2 OR or 3 AND.
. Type STEST to scatter copies of a snap, and ESC to stop it.
STEST=[CLEAR
BOX 0,0,20,20,3
BOX 5,0,10,15,2
BOX -5,0,10,15,1
SNAP IT,0,0,20,20
DISPLAY IT,-160%159,-100%100,0;SKIP 0]

. In the lesson you steer IT with the joystick by typing
. DISPLAY IT,X=X+$X1,Y=Y+$Y1,0;SKIP 0
. Type MOVEIT to do that, in fullscreen, with the arrow keys.
MOVEIT=[DISPLAY IT,X=X+$X1,Y=Y+$Y1,0;SKIP 0]

. A snap 4 pixels bigger than IT keeps a black border, which wipes out
. IT's trail as it moves.
SNAP IT,0,0,24,24

. DRAW's cursor is a snap shown twice in XOR, which draws it and takes
. it off again, so it flickers but never stays on the picture.
DRAW=[CLEAR
LINE 10,0,4
LINE -10,0,1
LINE 0,-10,4
LINE 0,10,1
SNAP CURS,0,0,20,20
X=X+$X1;Y=Y+$Y1
DISP CURS,X,Y,1;DISP CURS,X,Y,1
IF $T1==1,POINT X,Y,$K1/64+2
SKIP -3]

. Colormodes: 0-3 plop a color, 4-7 XOR it, 8-11 OR it, 12-15 AND it.
CLEAR
BOX 0,0,100,100,2
BOX 0,-25,50,50,1
BOX 0,25,50,50,3
BOX -25,0,50,50,9

. Swap colors 2 and 3 without redrawing anything.
A=$L2
$L2=$L3
$L3=A

BOX 0,0,100,100,1
BOX 0,-25,50,50,2
BOX 0,25,50,50,14
BOX -25,0,50,50,14

. Swap them back. $L2=$L3 would make colors 2 and 3 look the same.
A=$L2
$L2=$L3
$L3=A
. The lesson's NB is a system macro this emulator doesn't have.

JANEDRAW=[PROMPT "WHAT'S THE XSIZE,YSIZE OF THE
DRAWING BOX?"
INPUT WIZE,HIZE
PROMPT "WHAT'S THE SPACING FACTOR OF BOX CENTERS? (0
TO 10)"
INPUT SPACING
PROMPT "WHAT COLORMODE? (1 TO 15)"
INPUT KOLOR
PROMPT "CLEAR THE TV? (Y OR N)"
INPUT.STR ANSWER;IF ANSWER=='Y',CLEAR
PRINT "MOVE JOYSTICK KNOB TO POSITION, HOLD TRIGGER
TO DRAW"
X=0;Y=0
X=X+$X1*SPACING
Y=Y+$Y1*SPACING
BOX X,Y,WIZE,HIZE,7
BOX X,Y,WIZE,HIZE,7
IF $T1==0,SKIP -4
BOX X,Y,WIZE,HIZE,KOLOR;SKIP -5]

. BEHIND moves a box in XOR across lines: it passes behind the red ones
. and in front of the green.
BEHIND=[X=-100
Y=50
LINE X,Y,4
LINE X,-Y,2
IF (X=X+5)<51,SKIP -2
X=-100
BOX X,0,20,20,5
BOX X,0,20,20,5
IF (X=X+1)<51,SKIP -2]

. THE ANIMATION. BOUNCE makes STEST's picture with a black border round
. it, and bounces it off the edges of the screen. One DISPLAY draws the
. picture at its new place and its border wipes out the old one, so it
. never flickers. Press ESC to stop it.
BOUNCE=[CLEAR
BOX 0,0,20,20,3;BOX 5,0,10,15,2;BOX -5,0,10,15,1
SNAP BALL,0,0,26,26
CLEAR;X=0;Y=0;DX=3;DY=2
1GO DISPLAY BALL,X=X+DX,Y=Y+DY,0
IF X>144,DX=-3
IF X<-144,DX=3
IF Y>85,DY=-2
IF Y<-85,DY=2
WAIT 1;GOTO 1GO]
BOUNCE
